; bfsodium BLOCKKEEP : the ChaCha20 block  keeping the bytes it was made from
;
; HAND WRITTEN skeleton; The block function is PASTED from its own verified
; file; what is here is the copy that lets it be called more than once;
;
; INTERFACE entry=47 exit=64 footprint=0:335
; IO  in:  key{32}  ctr{4} LE  nonce{12}    (48 bytes)
;     out: keystream{64}  then the same forty eight bytes  unchanged
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x02f  saved{48}  key{32} @0x000  ctr{4} @0x020  nonce{12} @0x024;
;                 the caller puts them here once and they are still here after
;   @0x040:0x14f  the block routine's whole frame; blockloop runs at @0x040 and
;                 its footprint 0:271 is what sets the size of it; the forty
;                 eight bytes it works from go in at @0x050:0x07f and the
;                 keystream comes back at @0x040:0x07f
;   @0x0a0:0x0cf  copy temps{48}; these live INSIDE that frame  and are emptied
;                 before it is entered  which is what makes that safe
;
; blockloop CONSUMES the forty eight bytes it is given  which is right for a
; routine called once and wrong for a stream  where every block after the first
; wants the same key and nonce again and only the counter has moved; So they
; are kept at saved and copied in each time; The copy goes to the block's input
; AND to a temp in one pass  and the temp hands the original straight back;
;
; The temps sit inside the block function's own frame on purpose: there is no
; other free tape below it  and they are empty again before it is entered  so
; the cell it wants is the cell it gets;
;
; saved is at the BOTTOM of the tape and not above the frame  because a read
; prologue may hold only reads and single steps; a long run of steps before the
; first read is split across lines by the layout pass  and a paste starts at
; the prologue  so those steps would be silently dropped; tools/bffoot refuses
; a routine shaped that way  which is how this was found;

; read the key  the counter and the nonce into saved
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
; ASSERT ptr=47
; ASSERT zero 48:335
; to the head of saved
L47
; ASSERT ptr=0
  [-R80+R80+L160]
; the next byte
R1
  [-R80+R80+L160]
; the next byte
R1
  [-R80+R80+L160]
